    "created_at": "2022-12-09T09:53:22Z",
    "updated_at": "2022-12-09T09:53:22Z",
    "body": "Some thoughts:\r\n\r\n* This doesn't introduce the authority struct we discussed. It probably should to avoid having to change everything again in a follow-up PR? Or did you have another idea for that?\r\n* To keep the number of changes small and make review easier, we keep document's origin as a concept, but redefine it as returning document's policy container's authority's origin. Eventually we'll have to do replacements, but I suspect we rather want to have \"same authority\" (or some such) operations that take a document/settings object on one side (or both sides).\r\n* Depending on how many references there are to settings object's origin we do the same there, for now.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "reactions": {
